{{dokumentacija}}
&lt;!-- Categories go on the /doc subpage and interwikis go on Wikidata. --&gt;
&lt;/noinclude&gt;{{#invoke:etymology/templates|misc_variant_no_term|text={{glosar|{{#if:{{{nocap|}}}|i|I}}nternacionalizm}}|cat=internationalisms}}&lt;noinclude&gt;{{dokumentacija}}&lt;/noinclude&gt;{{#invoke:affix/templates|suffix}}&lt;noinclude&gt;{{dokumentacija}}&lt;/noinclude&gt;#WEITERLEITUNG [[Předłoha:sufiks]]{{spódk dokumentacije}}
{{skrót|Předłoha:suf}}
{{wužiwa lua|Modul:affix/templates}}
This template is used in the etymology section. Use

 {{předł|sufiks|&lt;var&gt;language code&lt;/var&gt;|&lt;var&gt;root&lt;/var&gt;|&lt;var&gt;suffix&lt;/var&gt;}}

where &lt;tt&gt;root&lt;/tt&gt; is the root of the term and &lt;tt&gt;suffix&lt;/tt&gt; is the suffix. For instance, a simple etymology of ''[[doing]]'' could be created with:

 {{předł|sufiks|en|do|ing}}

which evaluates to:

{{suffix|en|do|ing}}

== Other arguments ==
; {{para|sc}}
: Script code. See [[Wiktionary:Scripts]]
; {{para|t1}}, {{para|t2}}
: Glosses
; {{para|tr1}}, {{para|tr2}}
: Transliteration of word 1 and word 2 respectively (for non-Latin scripts)
; {{para|alt1}}, {{para|alt2}}
: Alternate text to display instead of the links.
; {{para|pos1}}, {{para|pos2}}
: Part-of-speech information.  Additional unquoted explanatory text, coming after the transliteration and gloss.
; {{para|id1}}, {{para|id2}}
: Sense ids
; {{para|lang1}}, {{para|lang2}}
: To use another language
; {{para|nocat|1}}
: Suppresses categorization

== See also ==
* {{předł|prefix}}
* {{předł|compound}}
* {{předł|confix}}
* {{předł|affix}}

